# Text is checked out as committed, with \n, on every system: the Makefile
# and shell scripts run under MSYS2 on Windows too, where Git would
# otherwise check text out with \r\n.
* text=auto eol=lf
# kept byte for byte: the .bgg reader's cases (crlf.bgg is \r\n on purpose)
# and the drift study's tables
*.bgg -text
*.csv -text
